    >>> x = jnp.array([0, 1, 2, jnp.nan, 3, 4, 5, 6])
    >>> q = jnp.array([25, 50, 75])

    Because of the NaN value, :func:`jax.numpy.percentile` returns all NaNs,
    while :func:`~jax.numpy.nanpercentile` ignores them:

